litedoc4 is Apache-2.0, and most of its dependency closure is dual-licensed
"MIT OR Apache-2.0": taking the Apache-2.0 option puts those crates under terms
LICENSE and this file already carry, which is why they are not listed here. The
crates below offer no such choice, so their own notices are reproduced.

This list is derived rather than curated. `tools/provenance-gate.sh` rebuilds it
from `cargo tree` over every target `release.yml` ships and fails if this section
and that closure disagree in either direction, so a new dependency cannot arrive
without its notice and a dropped one cannot leave a stale entry behind.

It covers the whole normal dependency closure, including crates that only run at
compile time. A proc-macro's own code is not linked into the binary, but the code
it generates is derived from it, and a notice printed for one crate too many
costs a paragraph while a missing one is an unmet obligation.

